                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h2]Review after 100% :[/h2]\nDo you like to waste time by watching paint dry?\nNo? \nIf so, then just look away, i'll save your time and say that this game is not for you.\n\nBut if somehow your answer is \"yes\" or \"maybe\" or perhaps you just want to hear more about what you can expect from this game, then these are the things that stand out about this game:\n\n[list]\n[*] Monotone autobattler gameplay reminisce of facebook idle flashgame but way worse.\n[*] Gameplay run at snail speed with no feature to speed it up with 2x or 3x speed setting.\n[*] Game will get paused if you alt+tab / click away from the window, forcing you to watch every single second of the super slow gameplay.\n[*] Every level is mind-numbingly long to the point that i lost count of how many time i fell asleep mid-battle.\n[*] You are forced to lvl speed in all your unit, not because it will increase dps, but because itll help you finish stage faster, otherwise you will lose more sanity.\n[*] You are forced to run the same stage over & over again to farm lvl for your unit so you can progress the story.\n[*] Game sometimes decide to crash right at the end of any stage (that already absurdly long) to make you question why you're still bothering with this game even more than before.\n[*] The whole forge system doesn't provide any description for weapons that you can make, there's no in-game guide, and the pdf guide on the dev site doesnt even include the final tier weapon (it cost so much that you'll spend hours just to be able to craft one and you wont know what it does until you crafted it).\n[/list]\n\nAll in all, it felt like total waste of a chore that will just eat your time and sanity. \n[spoiler]Trying to 100% this in a couple of days is lowkey some form of digital torture ngl.[/spoiler]",
